1
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Temaşevanên hêja, vê hefteya me berê xwe daye herêma Şiyê.
 
Dear viewers, this week we have turned our attention to the
Shiye region.

2
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Bernameya me jî îro li ser du gunda ye: Gundê Senarê û Gundê
Anqelê.
 
Our program today is about two villages: Senare Village and
Anqelê Village.

3
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Ev Gundê Senarê berî vê bi 500 sal da ava bûye...
 
This Senare Village was founded 500 years ago...

4
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
...û Gundê Anqelê jî berî vê bi 400 sal da ava bûye.
 
...and Anqelê Village was founded 400 years ago.

5
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Her gund 60 mal e. Her gundek 300 mal e...
 
Each village has 60 households. Each village is 300
households...

6
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Lê berî vê gundina çêbibin, li vir dibêjin Til Carnas.
 
But before these villages were built, they call this place
Til Carnas.

7
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Berî ew jî gundek bû. Berê milet li wir jî jiyan dikir.
 
Before that, it was also a village. People used to live
there too.

8
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Lê niha kes nemaye. Berî ev gundana çêbibin, ew gunda xera
bûbû.
 
But now no one remains. Before these villages were built,
that village was ruined.

9
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:22,000
318 hev dibe, û 10 pîr û dahn e.
 
It totals 318 [people], and 10 are elderly men and women.

10
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Lê ev gundana jî, ev du gundana edet û teqalîdê wan yek e...
 
But these villages too, these two villages, their customs
and traditions are one...

11
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
...goristana wan yek e, kaniya wan yek e, hemû tiştê wan yek
e.
 
...their cemetery is one, their spring is one, everything of
theirs is one.

12
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Lê ka em bi hevra derbas bin, em çanda her gunda nas bikin.
 
But let us proceed together, let us get to know the culture
of each village.

13
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Temaşevanên hêja, em derbasî Gundê Senarê bûn.
 
Dear viewers, we have entered Senare Village.

14
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Me got berî ku ev gunda ji berê Anqelê ava bûye.
 
We said before that this village was founded before Anqelê.

15
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Lê li vira Apê Şêx Salih li vira ye.
 
But here, Uncle Sheikh Salih is here.

16
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Emê pirsa ji wî pirs kin. Merheba.
 
We will ask him questions. Hello.

17
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Ehlen we sehlen. Hûn bi xêr hatin ser her du çava.
 
Welcome. You are welcome, upon both eyes.

18
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Em niha li mefreqa Gundê Senarê ne.
 
We are now at the intersection of Senare Village.

19
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Gundê Senarê gundekî qedîm e.
 
Senare Village is an ancient village.

20
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Yanê me got pênc sed sal da ava bûye?
 
Meaning, we said it was founded 500 years ago?

21
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:16,000
E, silef da, xiraban li jor hene, vêra dibên Xirabê 'Etarê.
 
Yes, on the slope, there are ruins up there, they call it
the Ruins of Atar.

22
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Malbetek hebûn digotin Malê Hemxêrê.
 
There was a family they called the Hemxêrê family.

23
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Ji vir va dûr e? Wê cîyê tê dibêyî?
 
Is it far from here? That place you are talking about?

24
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
E, pîçke dûr e. Di ciyê da ye.
 
Yes, it's a little far. It is in the mountainous area.

25
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Çend kîlometre hene?
 
How many kilometers are there?

26
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Yane sê kîlometre hene.
 
That is, there are three kilometers.

27
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Di wir da malbetek hebû digotin Malê Hemxêrê.
 
In there, there was a family they called the Hemxêrê family.

28
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Di wara Malê Xwêcelêra digotin.
 
Over there they called them the Xwêcelêr family.

29
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Dûra Mistê Hecî hat, gundek hebû navê xwa li Kurdistanê,
gundek heye navê xwa Senarê.
 
Then Mistê Hecî came, there was a village named in
Kurdistan, there is a village named Senare.

30
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Ji wa gundî hat, li vî derê li Xirabê rûnişt.
 
He came from that village, he settled here at the Ruins.

31
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Li Bakurê Kurdistan bû?
 
Was it in North Kurdistan?

32
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Belê, Bakurê Kurdistanê bû.
 
Yes, it was North Kurdistan.

33
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Li vî derê bû, hatin li vî derê peyman...
 
He was there, they came here [made a] treaty...

34
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Dûra hatin li va gundî şên kirin...
 
Then they came and populated this village...

35
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:05,000
...Mistê Hecî navê wê Senarê li va Senarê na.
 
...Mistê Hecî put the name of that Senare on this Senare.

36
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Şêx Salih, niha em li ber sînor in ne? Ev berxet in ne? Ev
gunda ji vir va dûr e?
 
Sheikh Salih, we are now near the border, right? These are
the borderlines? Is this village far from here?

37
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Dûr e. Gundê qedîm silef da dûr e ji vir va, dûr e.
 
It is far. The ancient village on the slope is far from
here, it is far.

38
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Li Bakur e.
 
It is in the North.

39
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Li vî derê ye. Navê wê Senarê li va Senarê na.
 
It is here. He put the name of that Senare on this Senare.

40
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Li vî derê curcumek heye, gelîk heye li vî derê, kaniya
Senarê vêra dibên, Geliyê Curcum.
 
There is a 'curcum' here, there is a valley here, the Spring
of Senare they call it, the Valley of Curcum.

41
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Curcumê mezin, Curcumê çûçik.
 
Big Curcum, Small Curcum.

42
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Curcumê mezin dîsa li Kurdistanê heye. Navê wê Curcumî li va
Curcumî na.
 
Big Curcum exists again in Kurdistan. He put the name of
that Curcum on this Curcum.

43
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Curcumê çûçik. Curcumê mezin heye, yê çûçik heye li vî derê
nan.
 
Small Curcum. Big Curcum exists, the small one is here.

44
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Aîle, li vî derê ra dibên aîle Mist Hecî a...
 
The family, around here they say the family of Mist Hecî
is...

45
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:57,000
...êd Malê de... Hemxêrê, êd Malê Reşîd, aîle. Aîle Malê
Xwêcelêra hene.
 
...those of the Hemxêrê family, those of the Reşîd family,
the family. There is the family of the Xwêcelêr.

46
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Aîle pir bûn, deha aîle zêde hene.
 
The families were many, there are more than ten families.

47
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Dûra aîle li vî derê, 17 mal bûn li Senarê.
 
Then the families here, there were 17 houses in Senare.

48
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Sê sed û pêncî sal gundê, va gunda yane şên bû.
 
Three hundred and fifty years this village, that is, was
populated.

49
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Xêrî... de li vî derê sed salî eyşîn, sed û pêncî salî
eyşîn, ez vira nizanim.
 
Besides... whether they lived here a hundred years, lived a
hundred and fifty years, I don't know that part.

50
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Li vî derê sînor tinebû. Alvêrê xwa, zewacî qîçkêd xwa diçûn
vî derê...
 
There was no border here. Their trade, the marriage of their
daughters, went here...

51
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:28,000
...Îskenderûnê dikirin, li Entakê dikirin. Alvêrê xwa Heleb
Melebê tinebû.
 
...they did in Iskenderun, they did in Antakya. Their trade
was not in Aleppo or such.

52
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Ev berê sînor daketî, ev gunda diçû şahî û pîgran...
 
Before the border went down, this village went to
celebrations and feasts...

53
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
...diçûn wê milî?
 
...they went to that side?

54
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Diçûn arê... diçûn ocê vî derê Kilis.
 
They went yes... they went to the side here, Kilis.

55
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Ew Îskenderûnê ye, diçûn Kilis jî. Kilis ha da.
 
That is Iskenderun, they went to Kilis too. Kilis is over
there.

56
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Diçûn alvêrê xwa li wira dikirin.
 
They went and did their trading there.

57
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Rehetî qîçkê xwa, zewacî qîçkê xwa li vî derê dikirin.
 
Their comfort of their girls, the marriage of their girls
they did here.

58
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Ji ber ku niha em çar kîlometre ji sînor va nîzîk in ne?
 
Because now we are four kilometers close to the border,
right?

59
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Yane berî vî miletî, ev gundana, ev gundê derdora sînor,
hemû diçûn wir da. Kes nizani Heleb çi ye yane.
 
That is, before this people, these villages, these villages
around the border, they all went that way. No one knew what
Aleppo was.

60
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Heleb kesî nizanîbû. Metelokek heye dibên...
 
No one knew Aleppo. There is a proverb they say...

61
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,000
...'Li gundê me rehmetî bûn, Heleb nedîn.'
 
...'In our village people passed away, they didn't see
Aleppo.'

62
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Ji va gundî mirin û çûn, Heleb nedîn.
 
From this village they died and went, they didn't see
Aleppo.

63
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,000
E, niha diçûn yane, va sînor der tinebû.
 
Yes, now they went, that is, that border barrier didn't
exist.

64
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Alvêr, git şitek li va... li Qirixxanê bûn, li Îskenderûnê
bûn, li Entakê bûn.
 
Trade, every single thing was at... at Kirikhan, at
Iskenderun, at Antakya.

65
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Bazarê me, alvêrê me, dewar, aliş-vêriş gişt li vî derê bûn.
 
Our market, our trade, livestock, buying and selling was all
here.

66
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Te spas dikim. Saet xweş.
 
I thank you. Good health [Thanks].

67
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, Xwedê û Pêxember ji we razî be,
serkeftin be ji we ra.
 
May God be pleased with you, may God and the Prophet be
pleased with you, success to you.

68
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Û Xwedê Rebûl Alemîn welatê me ava bike.
 
And may God the Lord of the Worlds build our country.

69
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Silavê me ji girtiyan re, ji serok û ji... hemû girtiyan re
hene.
 
Our greetings to the prisoners, to the leader and to... all
the prisoners.

70
00:08:42,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Spas.
 
Thanks.

71
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Temaşevanên hêja, li niha jî em gihîştin Gundê Anqelê.
 
Dear viewers, now we have arrived at Anqelê Village.

72
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Li vir jî civatek rûniştiye. Niha Apê Izet li kêlek min e.
 
Here too a gathering is seated. Now Uncle Izzat is by my
side.

73
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Apê Ezîz merhaba.
 
Uncle Aziz, hello.

74
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Merhaba.
 
Hello.

75
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Apê Ezîz, ev gundê we, kî têda avabûye? Ew destpêka tê kî
ye? Ev navê gundê we çi wext heye de dê?
 
Uncle Aziz, this village of yours, who founded it? Who was
the first? How long has this name of your village existed?

76
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Çar sed sal heye. Wexta ev gund şên kirin bira...
 
It has been four hundred years. When this village was
populated, brother...

77
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Kî hat destpêkê hat? Vira kî bû?
 
Who came at the beginning? Who was here?

78
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Yê hatine... Mala Mistehciyê bûn. Û Mala Elîkê bûn. Mala
Îmir bûn.
 
Those who came... were the family of Mistehecî. And the
family of Elîkê. The family of Îmir.

79
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Eee... Êş mala... Mala Se'dûn hebûn.
 
Eee... Also the family... The family of Sehdû (Se'dûn) were
there.

80
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Çar malbat bûn. Çar pênc bûn.
 
There were four families. Four or five.

81
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Yanî çar malbat vî gundî da jiyan dikirin berê?
 
So four families lived in this village before?

82
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

83
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Ev gundê we dibêjin berek kelek lê hebû.
 
They say your village used to have a fort.

84
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Kele hebû, erê. Kele hebû, kele hişta berê digotin kelata
dê.
 
There was a fort, yes. There was a fort, they used to call
it the Mother's Fort before.

85
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Na na, ev gundê we "Anqelê", çi wext heye vî navî? Ev nav çi
wext heye de dê?
 
No no, this village of yours "Anqelê", how long has it had
this name? How long has this name existed?

86
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Jimej e, hişta çar sed sal da ye.
 
It is ancient, it has been four hundred years.

87
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Erê, ev navê gundê we, nav, nav, çi me'ne dide?
 
Yes, this name of your village, name, name, what does it
mean?

88
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Me'neya xwe de em nizanin çi ye, me'neya xwe berê digotin
Anqelê. Anqelê.
 
Its meaning, we don't know what it is, its meaning... before
they said Anqelê. Anqelê.

89
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Na hine dibêjin navê gundê we, hinek dibêjin çîrokeke hene,
dibêjin "Anqelê" yanî "Kela Dayikê".
 
No, some say the name of your village, some tell a story,
saying "Anqelê" means "Mother's Fort".

90
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Hinek jî dibêjin dehe kelat li vir de hebûn, dibêjin "On
Kale". Navkî Tirkî yanî dibêjin.
 
Some also say there were ten forts here, saying "On Kale".
Meaning a Turkish name.

91
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Berê dîtin işte kele... "Anqelê", ya "dayikê".
 
Before they saw well the fort... "Anqelê", or "of the
mother".

92
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Û... Yek... Dehe, yanî berê digotin...
 
And... One... Ten, meaning before they said...

93
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
"On".
 
"On".

94
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
"On". Haa gotinek bi Tirkî yanî.
 
"On". Haa, a saying in Turkish, that is.

95
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Bi Tirkî yanî.
 
In Turkish, that is.

96
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Berê digotin dehe.
 
Before they used to say ten (deh).

97
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Na na ev gundê we û gundê Senarê va jî, yanî gund gihîştine
hevdu.
 
No no, this village of yours and the village of Senarê too,
meaning the villages have joined together.

98
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Gihîştine hevdu, gi meriyê hevdu ne.
 
They joined together, they are all relatives of each other.

99
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Yanî giş hevdu, zewicî ne, gi meriyê hevdu ne.
 
Meaning all together, intermarried, all relatives of each
other.

100
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Esasê xwe, em ji 'Etara bûn. Bavkê me, jime r'awil dan...
 
Its foundation, we were from Peddlers ('Etar). Our father,
passed down to us...

101
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Ku dere heev bû?
 
Where was he from?

102
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Haa Qereş kî, an jime bû... şerxî da ye.
 
Haa a Piastre (Qurûş), or from us... it's in the east
(şerxî).

103
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Yanî ji 'Etara paşê hatine vira.
 
Meaning from Peddlers then they came here.

104
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Û ew da milet dûre kom bûn û şên kirin.
 
And there the people gathered later and populated it.

105
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Evna dalbet bûn. Yek mala Eliyê axa bûn, yek jî mala me bûn,
pismamê hevdu bûn.
 
These were [dalbet]. One was family of Eliyê Axa, one was
our family, they were cousins.

106
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Na na, ew gundê we jî bi biyolî çandiniyê da, bi çi tê
naskirin?
 
No no, your village too regarding agriculture, what is it
known for?

107
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Çandiniyê da, çandiniya xwarinê da yanî, zira'etê xwe...
temam e, zira'etê.
 
In agriculture, in food agriculture, meaning, its
cultivation... is complete, cultivation.

108
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Na, dibêjin cee we, 'efrîn hemî bi zeytûna tê naskirin, bes
cee we jî bêtir bi zeytûnê Xelû tê naskirin.
 
No, they say your place, Afrin is all known for olives, but
your place is more known for Xelû olives.

109
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Zeytûnê Xelû, he. Zeytûnê Xelû, mala Xelû... Mala Xelû cee
me heye.
 
Xelû olives, yes. Xelû olives, the Xelû family... The Xelû
family has our place.

110
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Doxê... wey bi zeytûna pêda kirin...
 
[Unclear]... they grafted it with olives...

111
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Çawa bû? Çûne çi... qeleme hilkirin... sa kirin zeytûn e.
 
How was it? They went... lifted the scion... made it olive.

112
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Û çandin, hawna derketin. Xelû derketin. Nav lî nan mala
Xelû.
 
And planted, these came out. Xelû came out. Named after the
Xelû family.

113
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Ênê zeytûn, heta niha cee we hemî gi zeytûnê Xelû ne?
 
So the olives, until now your place are all Xelû olives?

114
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Xelû ne, Xelû bi jiyan e, zeytî jiyan e. Teşeyê baş in.
 
They are Xelû, Xelû is life, oil is life. They are good
quality.

115
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Erê, bes me got 'Efrîn hemî zeytûn in ne? Bes gundê we bi
taybet yanî...
 
Yes, but we said Afrin is all olives right? But your village
specifically...

116
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Xelû pir heye, erê.
 
Has a lot of Xelû, yes.

117
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Xelû pir lê heye.
 
Has a lot of Xelû.

118
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Waye, rast e.
 
That is so, it is true.

119
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Ez te spas dikim, saet xweş.
 
I thank you, have a good time.

120
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:16,000
A te jî xweş.
 
You too have a good time.

121
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Temaşevanên hêja, piştî me herdu gund derbas kirin, me çend
dave gundiyan naskirin.
 
Dear viewers, after we passed both villages, we met a few
villagers.

122
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Me got emê derbasî vê tilî jî bibin, Tilê Cirnas.
 
We said we would also pass by this hill, Tilê Cirnas.

123
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Belkî em binêrin kesek li wir hebe, dîroka vê tilî ji me re
xuyan bike.
 
Maybe we look if someone is there, to reveal the history of
this hill to us.

124
00:13:52,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Temaşevanên hêja, em gihîştin Tilê Cirnasê. Lê li pişt me
jî, bakurê Kurdistanê, ev gundê xuyan tên...
 
Dear viewers, we reached Tilê Cirnas. But behind us too,
Northern Kurdistan, these visible villages...

125
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Gundê Tûfan e... Gundê Sicê... Quruxanê... Ev çiyayê Gewr
e... Çiyayê Cirnasê ye...
 
Village of Tûfan... Village of Sicê... Quruxanê... This is
Mount Gewr... Mount Cirnas...

126
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Ev deşta Hemqê li piş me ye.
 
This Hemqê plain is behind us.

127
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Temaşevanên hêja, mirovekî vî gundî jî li vir e, ji gundê
Senarê, ew jî li vir e.
 
Dear viewers, a person from this village is also here, from
the village of Senarê, he is also here.

128
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Emê dîroka çiyayê... Tilê Cirnasê jê bipirsin. Merhaba ji te
ra.
 
We will ask him about the history of the mountain... Tilê
Cirnas. Hello to you.

129
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Tu bixêr hatî, ahlen we sehlen.
 
You are welcome, welcome.

130
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Navê te bi xêr?
 
Your name please?

131
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Kak 'Elî, çîroka vê tilî bêje, Tilê Cirnasê.
 
Mistefa 'Elî.

132
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Kak 'Elî, çîroka vê tilî bêje, Tilê Cirnasê.
 
Kak 'Elî, tell the story of this hill, Tilê Cirnas.

133
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Tilê Cirnasê, wele hevalê min î delal, wek em zanin û wek
jime r'e hewaldane mezinêt me.
 
Tilê Cirnas, well my dear friend, as we know and as the
elders passed down to us.

134
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Hev tilo, tilekî eserî ye. Destrûm têra derbas bûye. Qedîmen
kî têra derbas bûye.
 
This hill, is an artificial hill. Romans passed through it.
Ancient people passed through it.

135
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Bes ji sed sal û ez zanim, emrê min şêst û hinek e.
 
But for a hundred years that I know, my age is sixty and
some.

136
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Ji berê paşê da gavaniyê me li vira bûn. Û em jî dihatin ber
dewar, me li vir xew dikir şikefta da.
 
From back then our shepherdhood was here. And we came with
the cattle, we slept here in the caves.

137
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Şikeft û tişt tê da hene?
 
Are there caves and things in it?

138
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Wele de digotin sê sed, sê sed û çiqas o de nizanim, bîr û
serinc o şikeft o va...
 
Well they said three hundred, three hundred and something I
don't know, wells and cisterns and caves and such...

139
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Bes şikeftî haliyen, ê şexal ga gavana meselen pez dewerê
xwe dike, dehe dav sise ne. Serinc pir nixamtî ne.
 
But empty caves, that shepherds for example put their sheep
and cattle, there are ten, twenty, thirty. Cisterns are very
hidden.

140
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Û hev serincna jî, gişî av vedixwarniyan ê.
 
And these cisterns too, all drank water from them.

141
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Yanî berê digotin, li vê deştê hino digot xewna da dîtî av
heye.
 
Meaning before they said, on this plain some said in dreams
they saw water.

142
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Gê eger av li vê deştê heba, serinc nadatin kulan.
 
If there was water on this plain, they wouldn't have dug
cisterns.

143
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Yanî kanî tîne, li vir tu kanî tîne bûn?
 
Meaning springs, were there no springs here?

144
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Tîne. Kanî tîne ne. Esbeh serinc e vexwarina ne. Û vira
dibêjin Gola Hovo... Hav o gola.
 
None. No springs. It became cisterns for drinking. And here
they call Gola Hovo... That lake.

145
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Ê digotin binê... wekî Keferhece.
 
They said bottom... like Keferhece.

146
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Ê hevo... vira av têda diche dibû yanî kom dibû... ji dawara
xwe, pezê xwe av didan.
 
That one... here water collected in it, meaning gathered...
from their cattle, gave water to their sheep.

147
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Gava baran lê dikir av têda dibû gol, ji dawara xwe av didan
ê dewar. Ê vexwarinê ji serinca bû.
 
When it rained water became a lake in it, they watered the
cattle from it. The drinking was from cisterns.

148
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Û mal jî... li şîmal pir tîne ne, le'nû tizbîlaqe... vira
dibêjin tizbîlaq, kelimeya tizbî pir bi nav û deng e.
 
And houses too... in the north there are none, because
tizbîlaqe... here they call tizbîlaq, the word tizbî is very
famous.

149
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Û jiyî vir da, hevna gi mal in. Û ser til wek wadî ye,
qesrek spî hene 'amûd.
 
And from here on, these are all houses. And on the hill is
like a valley, there is a white palace, pillars.

150
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Le'nû esbeh... qesra padîşah li wir bû. Navê xwe Cirnas bû,
walîzalik nav Cirnas, Cirnas lînane, nav Cirnas bû.
 
Because it became... the king's palace was there. His name
was Cirnas, therefore name Cirnas, named Cirnas, name was
Cirnas.

151
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Û hew resmî... digotin ga ye. De ga ye, şêr e...
 
And that statue... they said it is a bull. It is a bull, a
lion...

152
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Ez dibêjim hewna jî 'îbadeta xwedayê wê çaxê bûye. Le'nû
berî vê da, 'îbadet ji seneman ra dikirin.
 
I say those were also worship of the god of that time.
Because before this, they worshipped idols.

153
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Hewa heykelê gindiyo bû. Û resmî qîşke jî hebû, asar hat
bir.
 
That was the statue of the village. And a statue of [qîşke]
also existed, the artifact was taken away.

154
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Û hev mentîqa jî, mentîqek meşhûr e bi zeytûna, mentîqa me
'Efrîn.
 
And this region too, a famous region for olives, our region
Afrin.

155
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Û îrada me û ê... mewsima vir jî reîsî zeytûn e.
 
And our will and the season here is principally olives.

156
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Haa, pê me hebî, naha dibêjin ev tila sal bi sal da tê.
 
Haa, behind us, now they say this hill is coming down year
by year.

157
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Da tê. Wa dibêjin, min tê bîra min, ser rast bû.
 
It is coming down. So they say, I remember, it was flat.

158
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Ê naha da ketiye. Ê min jî dî.
 
So now it has fallen. I saw too.

159
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Mm, da ketiye. De di bin da jî çi heye, ma ye'lemul xeybi
îlellah.
 
Mm, it has fallen. And underneath what is there, God only
knows the unseen.

160
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Binî jî çi heye em nizanin. Da dikeve.
 
Underneath what is there we don't know. It is falling.

161
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Û ha bajarra jî ez dibêjim, talama borkanî ye...
 
And these cities too I say, as long as it is volcanic...

162
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Doxê borkan rabûye... hev bajarê vira yî xera bûye.
 
A volcano rose... this city here was destroyed.

163
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Yanî ev berê milet li vir hebûn?
 
Meaning before people existed here?

164
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Milet hebû lo.
 
People existed lo.

165
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Berî ev dugundina ava bibin, milet li vir hebûn.
 
Before these two villages were built, people existed here.

166
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:10,000
Hebû lo, teb'en lo. Hev malina û hev serincna, gi milet li
vir hebû, gi qewm di 'eyşîn têda derbas bûn e.
 
Existed lo, naturally lo. These houses and these cisterns,
all people existed here, all tribes lived passed through
here.

167
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Ê gundê me teqrîben sê sed sal heye.
 
So our village is approximately three hundred years old.

168
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Sê sed, sê sed û pêncî sal ne, oo da ketin hatin e.
 
Three hundred, three hundred fifty years, oo they came down
came.

169
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Li viderê hebûn, hîn tirbê xwa li wî qiracî hane, vira
dibêjin Qiracê Rehve. Jêrî me ferê.
 
Over there existed, some of their graves are on that slope
there, here they call Qiracê Rehve. Below us.

170
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Qiracê Rehve giş xwaş xwaş hebûn. Giş tirbe bûn. Û li vir jî
tirbe hebûn. Esbeh ê vê tilî bûn.
 
Qiracê Rehve all were very good. All were graves. And here
too were graves. Probably they belonged to this hill.

171
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,000
Ez gelekî sipas dikim.
 
I thank you very much.

172
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Xwedê te bihêle. Ahlen we sehlen.
 
May God keep you. Welcome.

173
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Merhaba.
 
Hello.

174
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Ahlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

175
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Navê te bixêr?
 
Your name please?

176
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Usman.
 
Usman.

177
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Usman tu çend salî şivan î?
 
Usman how many years have you been a shepherd?

178
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Xwedê pênc şeş sal in.
 
By God five six years.

179
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Ê berî, berî te kî şivan bû ji malbata we?
 
So before, before you who was the shepherd from your family?

180
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,000
Bira kî min wala.
 
My brother really.

181
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Kê veyine?
 
Who else?

182
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Bavkê min, kalikê min. Ji berê da em şivan in.
 
My father, my grandfather. From before we are shepherds.

183
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Û ji ber da şivaniyê dikin yanî. Û timî tê vê Tilê Cirnasê?
 
And from before you do shepherding meaning. And you always
come to this Tilê Cirnas?

184
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Erê wala.
 
Yes really.

185
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Dengê te xweş e, tu stranekê ji me ra bêje.
 
Your voice is good, sing a song for us.

186
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Ez li vir xew dikim wala.
 
I sleep here really.

187
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Tu li vir xew dikî? Mala te li vir jî.
 
You sleep here? Your house is here too.

188
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Mm.
 
Mm.

189
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Tu bitenê tu, bavê xwe ver î?
 
You alone, with your father?

190
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Ez û bavê xwe bûn e.
 
Me and my father.

191
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Dibêjin dengê şivana pir xweş e. Tu zanî bistirê?
 
They say shepherds' voices are very good. Do you know how to
sing?

192
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

193
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Stranek. Tu kîjan strana, çi bistirê?
 
A song. You which song, what will you sing?

194
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Şitla.
 
Şitla (Sapling).

195
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Lê lê lê şitla minêêê... şitla minêêê... 'emrîyê moxorêêê...
şêrîna minêêê...
 
Le le le my sapling... my sapling... life of [moxorê]... my
sweet one...

196
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Ez dibêm çibkim ji te neavoot, ez kivoherim ji desta
xwedêêê...
 
I say what shall I do with you, I am a wanderer from God's
hands...

197
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Lê lê lê şitla minêêê... şitla minêêê... şêrîna minêêê...
'emrîyê moxorêêê... ez kivoherim ji desta xwedêêê...
 
Le le le my sapling... my sapling... my sweet one... life of
[moxorê]... I am a wanderer from God's hands...

198
00:18:52,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Ay saet xweş.
 
Ay, have a good time.

199
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Temaşevanên hêja, li vir jî Geliyê Curcumê ye. Li vira av
hebû. Li vira hemî kanî ne li vira.
 
Dear viewers, here is also the Valley of Curcum. Here there
was water. Here are all springs here.

200
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Gundê Senarê û Anqelê va, dihatin av ji vir dibirin.
 
The village of Senarê and Anqelê, came and took water from
here.

201
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Li vira jî, heft sala av hebû, heft sala jî dumiçiqî.
 
Here too, seven years there was water, seven years it dried
up.

202
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Yanî tu kanî çawa sa, ji me ra bêje çawa kanî li vir hebû?
 
Meaning you spring how, tell us how the spring existed here?

203
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Kanî, a reîsî, vêra dibêjin Kaniya Senarê, Anqelê, kaniya
mezin.
 
The spring, the main one, they call it the Spring of Senarê,
Anqelê, the big spring.

204
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Havoa reîsî bû, av... Senar, Anqelê giş texziye dikir.
 
That was the main one, water... Senar, Anqelê it supplied
all.

205
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Ji ava vexwarinê, kar û bar ra.
 
For drinking water, for work and business.

206
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Wekî didi hebûn... kanîkê... hw... hindik yanî, ava hindik
jê derdiketin.
 
Like there were two... springs... little meaning, little
water came out of them.

207
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Ew jî venadixwarin. Ava reîsî ji vê kaniyê bû.
 
That too they didn't drink. The main water was from this
spring.

208
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Û yek di l'derê wê da heye, vêra dibêjin Kaniya Baziyê, jê
bin zinêr av derdiket.
 
And one is outside of it, they call it Spring of Bazi, from
under the rock water came out.

209
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Şîniyê baziyê jê bin zinêr av derdiket.
 
Greenery of Bazi from under the rock water came out.

210
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Jê va nîzîk bî wan hat, jor ava xwedê digirtin dibirim.
 
They came near from there, they were taking God's water from
above and cutting it off.

211
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Li gundî Baziyê kîlak me li vir?
 
In the village of Baziye, which side is here?

212
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Erê, li vira hafê me ye.
 
Yes, here is our side/border.

213
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Şerqî me?
 
Our East?

214
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Na, dibêjin berê aş li vir hebûn.
 
No, they say there used to be mills here.

215
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Heft aş li ber vî gelî hebîn.
 
There were seven mills in front of this valley.

216
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ez navê aşvanan ji te ra xeber dim.
 
I will tell you the names of the millers.

217
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Kerem ke.
 
Please go ahead.

218
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Gundî Hisê, Elî Remedên...
 
Gundi Hise, Ali Remeden...

219
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Eh... Malê Elî Axa, Malê Mehmkê, Malê Îmir, Malê Ehmed
Axa...
 
Uh... The house of Ali Agha, the house of Mehmke, the house
of Imir, the house of Ahmed Agha...

220
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Malê... Tilyatê yekî da hebû.
 
The house of... Tilyat also had one.

221
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Heft ew li ber bûn. Heft aş li ber vê avê bûn.
 
There were seven in front. Seven mills were along this
water.

222
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Li ber vê avê hebûn?
 
They were along this water?

223
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Ber vê avê hebûn.
 
They were along this water.

224
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Na na, dibêjin ev kaniya heft salan hebû, heft sala jî
dimiçiqî.
 
No no, they say this spring existed for seven years, and for
seven years it would dry up.

225
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Ew gava dimiçiqî wa ji ku dibir?
 
When it dried up, where did you take [water] from?

226
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:55,000
O, bîrek li vira heye, bîrek ji mêj ve kolandî, di gwînê
Fransa da ye, gwînê Romanda.
 
Oh, there is a well here, a well dug a long time ago, in the
time of the French, in the time of the Romans.

227
00:20:55,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Kolana... ji wê av, bîra me av vedixwar Senar, anqelê
Baziyê.
 
Dug... from that water, our well from which Senar [village]
and the Baziye outpost drank.

228
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Dihatin ji wê bîrê av dikişandin vedixwarin.
 
They used to come and draw water from that well to drink.

229
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Û nahaw hîn bêliya şûnê kênder û zincîra têra hatiye
xwişandin devî se'rî ew bîrê bêliye.
 
And now the trace is still visible, the marks where the
ropes and chains rubbed against the mouth of the well are
visible.

230
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Av tê da heye?
 
Is there water in it?

231
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:19,000
Av di binî da heye, se... çîçkê xetimî ye, kevir der tê da
hene, gava derxînin ekîd avê derê.
 
There is water at the bottom, but... it's a bit blocked,
stones have fallen into it, if they clear it out, surely
water will come out.

232
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Ê tab ev kaniya çend sal e miçiqî ye dîsa?
 
So, for how many years has this spring been dried up again?

233
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Bi vira miçiqî ye.
 
It has been dry for a while here.

234
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Ev neha?
 
Right now?

235
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Neha. Ho sal miçiqî ye.
 
Now. It has been dry for years.

236
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Ho sal miçiqî? Sala çûyî hebû?
 
It has been dry for years? Was it there last year?

237
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Sala çûyî hebû.
 
Last year it was there.

238
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Bes kevir derketine... kevirên deryê ne, avê hebê belkim
noka jî hebe.
 
But stones have fallen... stones of the opening, if there is
water, maybe it is still there now.

239
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Temaşevanên hêja, ev bîra me behs jê dikir ev bîr e.
 
Dear viewers, this well we were talking about, this is the
well.

240
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Babê Ferîd ka tiştekî ji me ra li ser vê bîrê jî bêje.
 
Uncle Farid, tell us something about this well too.

241
00:21:54,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Ha bîra... bîra Romanî ye. Me çi waxt Senarê anqelê Baziyê
îstîmal dikirin.
 
This well... is a Roman well. For some time, Senar [village]
and the Baziye outpost used it.

242
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:08,000
Waxta kaniya Senarê anqelê hişk dibû, dihatin millet ji vê
bîrê av hildikişandin vedixwarin.
 
When the spring of the Senar outpost dried up, the people
would come and draw water from this well to drink.

243
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Ev ber vê bi çend sala ye?
 
How many years ago was this?

244
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Ji berî vê... bîr kolana bîrê zemanê Romaniya da hatiye
çêkirin.
 
From before this... the digging of the well was done in the
time of the Romans.

245
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Heta kengî we av ji vir dibir?
 
Until when did you take water from here?

246
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Haya ji berî vê deh donzdeh salan me dihat ji vira dibir.
Av.
 
Until ten or twelve years before this, we used to come and
take from here. Water.

247
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Nabera gundê we û bîra we çend kîlometre ye?
 
How many kilometers is it between your village and your
well?

248
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Teqrîben du kîlometre nîv hene.
 
There are approximately two and a half kilometers.

249
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,000
Te spas dikim, saet xweş.
 
Thank you, stay well.

250
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Ha te xweş.
 
You stay well.

251
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:49,000
Temaşevanên hêja, lejinên vî gundî jî xwestin xwarinê ji me
ra amade bikin.
 
Dear viewers, the women of this village also wanted to
prepare food for us.

252
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Lê neha emê bipirsin, bergî emê navê wan bipirsin. Navê te
bi xêr?
 
But now we will ask, first let's ask their names. What is
your name?

253
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Ezîze.
 
Azize.

254
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Fatma.
 
Your name?

255
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Fatma.
 
Fatma.

256
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Yê te?
 
Yours?

257
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Emîne.
 
Emine.

258
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Meta Ezîze, na ev xwarina we çi ye? Navê xwarinê çi ye, hûn
çi dikinê?
 
Aunt Azize, now what is this food of yours? What is the name
of the food, what do you put in it?

259
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Navê vê hevîrê ava germ e.
 
The name of this is "Hot Water Dough" (Hevîrê Ava Germ).

260
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Emê berî giyê bilxurê xwe bînin, avê xwe jî germ bikin.
 
First we bring our bulgur (cracked wheat), and we heat our
water.

261
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Emê dînin, avê xwe lêkin û tiştê xwe jî gî pê werkin,
bîbera, kemûna xwe ye...
 
We put it down, pour our water on it, and add all our things
to it, the pepper, our cumin...

262
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Emê gî pê werkin û çîçkê bêlin.
 
We mix it all in and let it sit a little.

263
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Pîvazên xwe jî em diqelînin, didin niyalîkî.
 
We fry our onions, putting them aside.

264
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:22,000
Ba'dî fetrekê emê derxin, bistirên, bistirên...
 
After a period, we take it out, knead it, knead it...

265
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Û pîvazê xwe jî biwuşkin nav û zeytê.
 
And we toss our onions in butter and oil.

266
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:29,000
Û cimka çêkin û têkin sena û bextenîsê xwe jî pê werkin.
 
And we make small balls and put them on the tray, and add
our parsley to it.

267
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Û deynin xwarinê.
 
And set it out to eat.

268
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Ev naçe ser êgir?
 
Does this not go on the fire?

269
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:36,000
Na, bes ava germ ku pê nerm bike, bes.
 
No, just the hot water to make it soft, that's all.

270
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:37,000
Bes ava germ?
 
Just hot water?

271
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Teuka, em niha çawa çêdikin.
 
Look now, how we are making it.

272
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Em çêkin.
 
We are making it.

273
00:24:40,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Temaşevanên hêja, emê li gel hev ra temaşe bikin.
 
Dear viewers, let's watch together.

274
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Temaşevanên hêja, li vir jî bi dawî bû.
 
Dear viewers, it is finished here too.

275
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Na ji min ra bêje, dibêjin hevîr gelek in. Ka navê wan bêje
ji min ra, çend hevîr hene?
 
Now tell me, they say there are many [types of] doughs. Tell
me their names, how many doughs are there?

276
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Wa... heva hevîrê ava germ e.
 
This... this is Hot Water Dough.

277
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:41,000
Yê ava sar heye. Yê hevîrê nîskê heye.
 
There is Cold Water [dough]. There is Lentil Dough.

278
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Û de Ereb jî dibên kibbe neye, ab gûşt heye.
 
And the Arabs also call it Kibbeh Nayyeh (Raw Kibbeh), there
is the one with meat.

279
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:49,000
Û kibbe bi derewîş heye, kibbe bi lebeniyê heye, kibbe bi
sîniyê heye, pir in.
 
And there is Dervish Kibbeh, Yogurt Kibbeh, Pan Kibbeh,
there are many.

280
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,000
Bi enwae.
 
Of all kinds.

281
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Ê cem Efrînê sisisê ne?
 
Are there three types for Afrin?

282
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Ê Efrînê, yê nîskê ye, û yê ava germ, yê ava sar.
 
For Afrin, it is the lentil one, and the hot water one, the
cold water one.

283
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Û hevîr, no dibên kufte, kufte jî hene.
 
And dough, now they call it Kufte, there are Kuftes too.

284
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Destê te sax bin.
 
Health to your hands.

285
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:20,000
Saet xweş.
 
Stay well.

286
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:44,000
Temaşevanên hêja, li vî gundê Senarê jî me necarek dî.
 
Dear viewers, in this village of Senar we also saw a
carpenter.

287
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Necarê jî 43 sal, 44 sal li vî karî dike, lê tenbûra jî
çêdike.
 
This carpenter has been doing this work for 43, 44 years,
but he also makes Tanburs [musical instruments].

288
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Ne bes necarleqê dike, tenbûra jî çêdike.
 
Not only does he do carpentry, he makes Tanburs too.

289
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Mamosta Omer, merheba.
 
Master Omer, hello.

290
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,000
Ehlen we sehlen, ser çavê min.
 
Welcome, upon my eyes.

291
00:26:56,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Çavê te sax be. Na na, micarî ne di ye, necar û yek tenbûra
çêke bi hev ra kar bike.
 
May your eyes be healthy. Now, carpentry isn't just... a
carpenter and one who makes Tanburs working together.

292
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Te çawa ev kara bi hev ra girt? Yanî hinda necar te qapiya
çêdikir, tu hinda tenbûra çêdikeyî?
 
How did you combine these works? Meaning, doing carpentry
you made doors, and you make Tanburs?

293
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:12,000
Wele birayê delal, xandî meraqê sêz bû, fen bû min girt.
 
Well my dear brother, since childhood it was a passion, an
art that I picked up.

294
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:16,000
Min meraq kir, ka ez vê saziyê çêkim, ez bi xwe hîn bûm.
 
I had a passion, [I said] let me make this instrument, I
learned it by myself.

295
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Û ez belakim nav millet, ji gelek ji millet ra yane.
 
And I distribute it among the people, for many of the
people.

296
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Yanî pêşiya te kesî çêdikir tenbûr?
 
Meaning, did anyone make Tanburs before you?

297
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:27,000
Kesî çênekir. Min di dilê xwe da, di serê xwe da, di mêjiyê
xwe da min meraq kir û min çêkir.
 
No one made them. In my heart, in my head, in my brain, I
had the passion and I made it.

298
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Ez cem kesî, min kar nekir yanî, neşuxulî me.
 
I didn't work with anyone, I wasn't employed [by others to
learn].

299
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:32,000
Te necarleqê dikir?
 
Did you do carpentry?

300
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:39,000
Necarleqê dikir, hûrik hûrik, o pê ra min qundaqên sîlaha
min çêkirin.
 
I did carpentry, bit by bit, and then I made gun stocks.

301
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Çûyê dikala min çêkirin.
 
I made plow handles.

302
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Eh her tiştê ku gerekê millet bû, min jê ra çêkir û
qedimandin yane.
 
Whatever was needed by the people, I made for them and
provided.

303
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Ê de ka ji me ra bêje, bi yek yek bêje çi û çi te çêdikir?
 
So tell us, tell us one by one what exactly you made?

304
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Wele ez tenbûra çêdikim.
 
Well, I make Tanburs.

305
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:57,000
Û qapî û pêncera min çêdikirin.
 
And I made doors and windows.

306
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Textê reş min çêdikirin.
 
I made blackboards.

307
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Qundaqên sîlaha min çêdikirin.
 
I made gun stocks.

308
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Gerekê şebab, millet bûn min çêdikirin.
 
Whatever the youth, the people needed, I made.

309
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:10,000
Her tiştê kî yane ku gerekê millet, û millet pê hewce ye,
min jê ra çêkir û min jê ra qedimandin yane.
 
Everything that the people needed, and the people were in
need of, I made for them and provided for them.

310
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:12,000
Tu tu caran ji gund derneketî, te derneketî?
 
You never went out of the village, you didn't leave?

311
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:15,000
Na, qet derneketim. Ez nav milletê xwe, ji nav gundê xwe
derneketim.
 
No, never left. I never left my people, never left my
village.

312
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:17,000
Temam. Yanî te ji strana pir hez dikir?
 
Okay. So you loved songs a lot?

313
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:19,000
Pir hez dikir, û ev xweşî yane...
 
Loved it a lot, and this goodness...

314
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Te guhdariya kê dikir?
 
Who did you listen to?

315
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:27,000
E... bi şeklekî am, yane millet, ê distirê, ê dengbêj min
guh lê dida yane.
 
Uh... generally speaking, the people, the singer, the bard,
I listened to them.

316
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Ji dengê wî min hez dikir.
 
I loved their voice.

317
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Wek kê?
 
Like who?

318
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Wekî Mihemedê Elî Tijo, Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke, hazir û xeyb.
 
Like Mhemedê Elî Tijo, may God have mercy on him, present
and absent.

319
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:37,000
Wekî Bavê Piling Cemîl Horo.
 
Like Bavê Piling Cemîl Horo.

320
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Û pê ra, sazkarên me kurda pir bûn.
 
And besides, our Kurdish artists were many.

321
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Teben en Evdê Şe're, û Hesen Nazî, wana em negihîştinê.
 
Of course, ones like Evdê Şe're and Hesen Nazî, we didn't
catch them [live in their time].

322
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Bes gotinêt wana me di tecîla da bîst û me guh lê dan û me
jê hez kirin yane.
 
But we heard their sayings in recordings and we listened to
them and loved them.

323
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Temam, no te tenbûr cem te hene? Te çêkirine?
 
Okay, now do you have Tanburs with you? Have you made them?

324
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,000
Hene.
 
There are.

325
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:55,000
Ha we tenbûra...
 
This Tanbur here...

326
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,000
Ji darê tûyê ye.
 
Is from mulberry wood.

327
00:28:57,000 --> 00:29:01,000
Çêkirina min e, hewa şuxulê destê min e, di sala...
 
It is my make, this is my handiwork, in the year...

328
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:03,000
Sala heftê û hefta da.
 
In the year seventy-seven.

329
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Di bîst û pêncî Temûzê min çêkir.
 
On the twenty-fifth of July I made it.

330
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Na tenbûr bes ji darê tûyê têne çêdibê?
 
Now, are Tanburs only made from mulberry wood?

331
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:10,000
Na, ji pir dara çêdibe.
 
No, it is made from many woods.

332
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Ji darê tûyê, e... yeka, yane newa yeke.
 
From mulberry wood, uh... that is one, meaning type one.

333
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:19,000
Ê didiyê, evirse.
 
The second one, Juniper (Evirse).

334
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Û pê ra darê, darê mişmişê, darê behîvê.
 
And then wood... apricot wood, almond wood.

335
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Her darekî sert, wek gotinê di...
 
Any hard wood, as is said in...

336
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Na bi zimanê me dibên, darê req.
 
Not in our language, they say 'darê req' [hard wood].

337
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,000
Bi Erebî dibên xeşeb el qasî.
 
In Arabic they say 'khashab al-qasi' [hard wood].

338
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Ji darê mekin tenbûr çêdibe.
 
Tanbur is made from solid wood.

339
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Bes ê herî xweş, dengî xwe, dengê henûn?
 
But the best one, its sound, the sweet/gentle sound?

340
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Darê evirse baş e.
 
Juniper (Evirse) wood is good.

341
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Ê evirse baş e.
 
The Juniper is good.

342
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Başê, başê sêzgî ye.
 
It is good, good for the instrument.

343
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Paşê ji wî ro tûyê, darê tûyê ye.
 
After that comes mulberry, mulberry wood.

344
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Tu bi xwe strana jî dibêjî? Tu dengbêjî?
 
Do you sing yourself? Are you a bard?

345
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Wele, heseb xwesteka, min dil...
 
Well, depending on the request, [if] my heart...

346
00:29:54,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Jiber ku te got ez gelek meraqê, elbesta bûm, û strana bûm,
û muzîkê, muzîka Kurdî bûm.
 
Because you said I was very passionate about costumes/poems,
and songs, and music, Kurdish music.

347
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Weh weh weh, çiqas xweş ez ê bibêjim.
 
Wow wow wow, how beautifully I will sing.

348
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Gerê me dîya, dilê wan kervan e, dilê min dêr e, seyrî dêr
e.
 
I wandered and saw, their hearts are caravans, my heart is a
church, a sight of a church.

349
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Wan ê dilê min dêr e, seyrî dêr e.
 
Oh, my heart is a church, a sight of a church.

350
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Bêlê anê mîla rohilatê, şewqa Xwedê da, wel wel anê roja bi
xêr e.
 
Yes mother, the light of the east, God gave the glow, oh
mother, it is a blessed day.

351
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:09,000
Mîla şewq û şemala xwe da her çar goşê dunê.
 
The shaft of light gave its glow and candle to all four
corners of the world.

352
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Bi ser ra keleha Mêrdînê heta bajarê Wêranşarê.
 
Over the Citadel of Mardin, up to the city of Viransehir.

353
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:19,000
Cî û merkezê Teyr Begê, lawikê lewend paşa, anê mîla bida
pûç î dunê re.
 
The place and center of Teyr Beg, the handsome pasha boy,
mother, let the light shine on this vain world.

354
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:28,000
Bêlê anê mîla şewq û şemala xwe da bajarê Urfê li cem meqamê
Ebû Muslimê Teberdar e.
 
Yes mother, the shaft of light gave its glow and candle to
the city of Urfa, near the shrine of Abu Muslim the Ax-
bearer.

355
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Anê ya jikî bajarê Urfê berî jêr e, rizqê ya jikî tehsilkirî
bi şilf û darê erjê veger e.
 
Mother, one is from the city of Urfa facing south, the
other's sustenance is collected, returning from the land
with bare weapons.

356
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Bêlê anê mîla dîsa şewq û şemala xwe da...
 
Yes mother, again the shaft of light gave its glow and
candle...

357
00:31:46,000 --> 00:32:00,000
... serê serhedê, pozê zozana, banda Bîngolê, bav û bi
delal, bi mêrg û bi kanî ye, bi çawîr û bi çîman e, car da
car da cimezganî kî bi xêr e.
 
... to the top of the borderlands, the peak of the plateaus,
the side of Bingol, father and dear, with meadows and
springs, with pastures and grass, time and again a blessed
gathering.

358
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Gelek spas, spas ji bo dengê te yî xweş.
 
Thank you very much, thanks for your beautiful voice.

359
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Temaşevanên hêja, îro me li du gundan derbas kir. Gundê
Senarê û gundê Anqelê.
 
Dear viewers, today we spent time in two villages. The
village of Senar and the village of Anqel.

360
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:42,000
Li hemî xatirê xwe ji we dixwazin, ka heya bernameyek din,
li cîkî din, emê dîsa bi hev ra bin.
 
We bid you all farewell, until another program, in another
place, we will be together again.

